# Normalise line endings so `git status` reflects real changes.
#
# Without this, 97 files showed as modified on a clean checkout: the working
# tree held CRLF, the index held LF, and git reported every one of them as
# changed. Every review of "which files did this batch touch?" started by
# filtering that noise out, and twice it hid a real change inside it.
#
# `text=auto` lets git decide per file and store LF in the repository.
# Checkout still gets the platform's native endings, so nothing changes for
# an editor on Windows.
* text=auto

# Explicitly text, whatever heuristics would say.
*.py     text
*.md     text
*.yml    text
*.yaml   text
*.json   text
*.feature text
*.ini    text
*.txt    text
*.cfg    text

# Binary: never touched, never diffed as text.
*.png    binary
*.jpg    binary
*.zip    binary
*.pptx   binary
*.docx   binary
*.pdf    binary
*.trace.zip binary
